hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2731","Narrated to us Abd al-Aziz ibn Ahmad ibn Suwayd, Abu Amirah al-Balawi, the mu'adhdhin of the Mosque of Ramla: He narrated to us Ayyub ibn Suwayd, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Musaf' al-Hajbi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (RA), who reported that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The Black Stone (al-Rukn) and the Station of Ibrahim (al-Maqam) are two rubies from the rubies of Paradise. Allah has effaced their light"," and were it not for that"," they would have illuminated everything between the east and the west.\""\n\nAbu Bakr said: This report has not been narrated by anyone more knowledgeable of its chain than al-Zuhri except Ayyub ibn Suwayd"," provided he preserved it accurately from him. It has also been narrated as a marfu' report from Musaf' ibn Shaybah"," not via al-Zuhri"," by Rajah Abu Yahya."""
"2732","###\n Al-Hasan az-Za'farani narrated to us, saying: Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, saying: Raja' Abu Yahya narrated to us, saying: Musafi' bin Shaybah said: I heard Abdullah bin 'Amr (RA) saying: He swore by Allah three times, and placed his two fingers in his ears, saying: \I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'Indeed"," the Black Stone and the Maqam (Station of Ibrahim)...'\"" (He said the rest of the"""
